{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00470",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.36,
      "end_seconds": 6.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, I couldn't find the door at first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.14,
      "end_seconds": 11.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.04,
      "end_seconds": 24.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "Oh, you know, honestly, it's irregular periods, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.75,
      "end_seconds": 28.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Mm. On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.84,
      "end_seconds": 48.43,
      "duration_seconds": 17.59,
      "text": "About a six out of ten. Right, as for excess hair on my face, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. And acne along the jaw, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.39,
      "end_seconds": 54.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.81,
      "end_seconds": 64.34,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago. I stay with my daughter and her family. I'm mostly vegetarian."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.03,
      "end_seconds": 81.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.2,
      "end_seconds": 87.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Dust. I come out in... well, itchy eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.32,
      "end_seconds": 92.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.23,
      "end_seconds": 97.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "I had a C-section about ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.67,
      "end_seconds": 100.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Any diagnoses you've been given before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.31,
      "end_seconds": 129.3,
      "duration_seconds": 24.99,
      "text": "Um, I've had COPD, yes. I did try to ignore it for a while. I've got diabetes. It's the not knowing that gets to me. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. Yes, high blood pressure. I have an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.77,
      "end_seconds": 132.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Okay, and what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.62,
      "end_seconds": 139.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Yes, COPD is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.69,
      "end_seconds": 153.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.0,
      "end_seconds": 165.35,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "I take Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest. I take Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.88,
      "end_seconds": 168.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.18,
      "end_seconds": 178.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "About two years. It's, It's losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.25,
      "end_seconds": 180.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.66,
      "end_seconds": 191.51,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid. Before this I was on glimepiride; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.15,
      "end_seconds": 211.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "A few quick ones: milk from the breasts or heavy bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.37,
      "end_seconds": 215.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.9,
      "end_seconds": 216.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "And then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.52,
      "end_seconds": 224.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Any trying for a baby, pelvic pain or headaches with vision changes at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.35,
      "end_seconds": 236.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.5,
      "text": "No trying for a baby, pelvic pain or headaches with vision changes, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.38,
      "end_seconds": 240.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.36,
      "end_seconds": 243.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.99,
      "end_seconds": 248.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.4,
      "end_seconds": 257.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.36,
      "end_seconds": 273.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 112 over 79, respiratory rate 14, temperature 36.5, heart rate 86."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.71,
      "end_seconds": 280.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.83,
      "end_seconds": 283.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Alright, that's fine, we'll come to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.95,
      "end_seconds": 289.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Right, let me check a few things physically."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.29,
      "end_seconds": 293.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Stay still while I have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.9,
      "end_seconds": 317.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Facial acne along the jaw and some dark coarse hair on the chin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.31,
      "end_seconds": 335.02,
      "duration_seconds": 13.71,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit up. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with possible polycystic ovary syndrome at this stage. A thyroid problem is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.84,
      "end_seconds": 339.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.66,
      "end_seconds": 354.31,
      "duration_seconds": 13.65,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now possible polycystic ovary syndrome is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let's book hormone blood tests to look into irregular periods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 355.53,
      "end_seconds": 360.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "We have a slot Tuesday at 2 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.05,
      "end_seconds": 375.38,
      "duration_seconds": 14.33,
      "text": "I'm going to order a thyroid test, for irregular periods. Regular exercise and modest weight loss can bring cycles back. Please come and see me after the results are back. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.45,
      "end_seconds": 382.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Uh, thanks so much, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.22,
      "end_seconds": 386.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Mind how you go."
    }
  ]
}